### The open core's words in English: the emails it sends (the layout
### every email shares, and the password reset). Every message has a note
### above it: where it shows, who reads it, and what each variable holds.

## Every email

# The button's words when an email names no other.
email-cta-default = Open Flash
# Above the button's address, written out for clients that hide buttons.
email-paste-link = Or paste this link into your browser:
# The footer's line for questions. $email is the support address (a
# link); keep the markup as it is.
email-questions-html = Questions? Reply to this email, or write to <a href="mailto:{ $email }" style="color:#6d6d75;">{ $email }</a>.
# The same line in the plain-text part. $email is the support address.
email-questions-text = Questions? Reply to this email, or write to { $email }

## Resetting a password

# The email's subject, and its title.
email-reset-subject = Reset your Flash password
# The preview line mail apps show beside the subject.
email-reset-preheader = Set a new password. The link works once and expires in 1 hour.
# The email's heading.
email-reset-heading = Reset your password
# The email's first line.
email-reset-body = Someone (probably you) asked to reset the password for this Flash account.
# The button.
email-reset-cta = Set a new password
# Under the button.
email-reset-expiry = The link works once and expires in 1 hour.
# The footer's note.
email-reset-ignore = If you didn't ask for this, ignore this email. Nothing changes, and your current password keeps working.
# Plain-text part: before the link.
email-reset-here = Set a new password here:
# Plain-text part: after the link.
email-reset-text-end = The link works once and expires in 1 hour. If this wasn't you, ignore this email. Nothing changes.
